From d1533ed8357c1f57d1e8054cc70f041f71711c70 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 18:37:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] kernel: pin arm64 to 7.3.3-sky1-ncz (r298), retire
 7.3.1-sky1-ncz

7.3.3-sky1-ncz r298 (v7.3.3 d50d994bffa3, meta-cix kb/sky1-7.3.3-r298-20261107
ec3bacd1, the 7.3.1 series unchanged, 33 patches) passed the O6N boot test on
@O6N_BOOT_DATE@, so it becomes the arm64 CURRENT kernel; arm64 and amd64 now pin the
same 7.3.3.

Staged release kernel-staging/r298-7.3.3-sky1-ncz-20261107 (mainline.release);
mainline.deb-revision is removed (the release carries its own revision).
Image f47b74e2..., vmlinux build id 19c5ddd7..., 376 uncompressed modules,
six overlays rebuilt against the r298 Module.symvers (already in
assets/kernel/<drv>/7.3.3-sky1-ncz). linux-image-cixmini f53d7ed0...,
linux-headers-cixmini e8286ae5..., cixmini-boot 1.6+r298 0cf4e780....
build-kernel-debs.sh freezes the r298 deb epoch (1793607971, the epoch the
pinned debs were built with).

KERNEL-LIFECYCLE: CURRENT arm64 7.3.3-sky1-ncz / 7.3.3-sky1-ncz+r298, RETIRED
adds 7.3.1-sky1-ncz. kernel-manifest.json regenerated (kernel-manifest.py gen),
sky1-manifest.json, ledger rows, components.tsv (regenerated) and the
determinism.pin ledger digest follow.
---
 assets/kernel-manifest.json         |  26 +++----
 assets/kernel/KERNEL-LIFECYCLE      |  13 ++--
 assets/kernel/KERNEL-POLICY         |   3 +-
 assets/kernel/mainline.deb-revision |  13 ----
 assets/kernel/mainline.release      |   2 +-
 assets/kernel/sky1-manifest.json    | 108 +++++++++++++---------------
 build/build-kernel-debs.sh          |   1 +
 manifests/components.tsv            |  14 ++--
 manifests/determinism.pin           |   2 +-
 manifests/ncz-packages.tsv          |   6 +-
 10 files changed, 84 insertions(+), 104 deletions(-)
 delete mode 100644 assets/kernel/mainline.deb-revision

